{
  "id": "27887_gaisuru",
  "headword": "害する",
  "reading": "がいする",
  "romaji": "gaisuru",
  "part_of_speech": "suru verb",
  "gloss": "to harm; to injure; to damage",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to harm; to injure; to damage; to hurt (feelings, health)",
      "explanation": "To cause harm or damage to something, especially health, feelings, or interests. Common in formal or written contexts and in fixed expressions."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27887_gaisuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{健康|けんこう}を{害|がい}する。",
      "english": "It harms your health.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27887_gaisuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "そんな{言|い}い{方|かた}では{相手|あいて}の{気分|きぶん}を{害|がい}する。",
      "english": "Putting it that way will offend the other person.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27887_gaisuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{過度|かど}の{飲酒|いんしゅ}は{健康|けんこう}を{害|がい}するおそれがある。",
      "english": "Excessive drinking can damage your health.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n- Transitive ({他動詞|たどうし}); what is harmed is marked with を.\n- Pattern: [thing]を{害|がい}する\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {健康|けんこう}を{害|がい}する: to damage one's health\n- {気分|きぶん}を{害|がい}する: to offend; to put in a bad mood\n- {感情|かんじょう}を{害|がい}する: to hurt someone's feelings\n- {利益|りえき}を{害|がい}する: to harm someone's interests\n\nREGISTER: Formal and somewhat literary; in casual speech {傷|きず}つける (to hurt) or {悪|わる}くする is more common.",
